## Why each class S edit holds the same strength

- Week 404: the old row held two texts; the new row holds two texts, the 404 status, the locale
  language, the highest open week read from the loaded content, and a 48 px link (new). The
  `/th/nowhere` self-test keeps the `old` variant, so the language half still runs.
- Tap targets: the old row held one 44 px floor over one selector. The new row holds the 44 px
  floor over every control and bounds the accepted word exception by count, by the presence of
  the pseudo hit area, and by a 10 x 36 px floor per word, and it fails on a reader page with no
  words (`words=0` there is a failure).
- Hover: the old row measured one hover state. The new row measures the hover state of a real
  target and fails when the fixture holds none, so it is not weaker.
- Word cut rows: the old rows measured the pause time of a behavior that AC-1.12 deleted. The
  new rows hold the three clauses of AC-1.12: the own clip, no seek, no stop, and the no-clip
  rule.

## Deviations recorded

1. The orchestrator allowed the script rows as an edit path for this triage. The commit holds the
   script only.
2. The commit subject from the handoff is 102 characters; the commitlint header limit is 100. The
   subject is `test(storytime): update the phase 3 gate rows for look changes (track_id: storytime_look_20261107)`
   (98 characters, same intent).
3. The gate's sign-in helper now posts with the origin of its own request. An uncommitted change of
   the login track (`lib/auth/same-origin.ts`, `ownOriginOf`) compares the `Origin` header to the
   `Host` header, so the fixed `http://localhost:<port>` origin answers 403 against the
   `127.0.0.1` bind (`Error: sign-in of staff-01 gave status 403`). That line belongs to the login
   track; the orchestrator can move it.
4. The fixture adds `wordClips` for the w01 readalong book (all words except `i`), because the
   shipped week holds no clips and AC-1.12 rows would have no target. The fixture copy is part of
   the script; the shipped file is untouched.

## Remaining failures (class X, login track)

`all_controls_visible` fails on the week, decodable, and song screens at 844x390. The control out
of view is `button[ออกจากระบบ]` (the sign-out form of `page.tsx:453`, commit `ef36b6c37`). The
reader and question screens pass. The look phase 1 browser gate row 4 measures horizontal page
overflow (`page_overflow=0`) at phone landscape; that row passes. No look AC asks to move the
sign-out control, and the control is not child-facing.

